[44.228093, "o", "I have everything I need. Here is the full preflight report:\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Preflight Qualification Report\r\n\r\n### 🔴 Verdict: BLOCK — upgrade must NOT proceed\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Key Metadata\r\n\r\n| Field | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| **Verdict** | `BLOCK` |\r\n| **Fingerprint** | `80483bd4091749dd` (first 20 chars: `80483bd4091749dd4b4f`) |\r\n| **Tool** | helm-agent-preflight v0.1.0-dev |\r\n| **Timestamp** | 2026-11-13T01:57:52Z |\r\n| **No deployment occurred** | ✅ Confirmed (`true` in both `operation` and `run_metadata`) |\r\n| **Evidence completeness** | `COMPLETE` (no limitations) |\r\n| **Rendering stability** | ✅ Confirmed |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Security Findings\r\n\r\n#### [CRITICAL] RBAC-001 — Wildcard resources (NEW)\r\n\r\n| Field | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| **Object** | `ClusterRole / demo-app-reader` |\r\n| **Path** | `$.rules[0].resources` |\r\n| **Message** | wildcard (`*`) in resources grants access to all resource types |\r\n| **Pre-existing** | `false` — **introduced by this upgrade** |\r\n| **Verdict contribution** | BLOCK |\r\n\r\n#### [CRITICAL] RBAC-002 — Wildcard verbs (NEW)\r\n\r\n| Field | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| **Object** | `ClusterRole / demo-app-reader` |\r\n| **Path** | `$.rules[0].verbs` |\r\n| **Message** | wildcard (`*`) in verbs grants all operations |\r\n| **Pre-existing** | `false` — **introduced by this upgrade** |\r\n| **Verdict contribution** | BLOCK |\r\n\r\nBoth findings are **new** — the baseline was clean. This upgrade introduces them.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Diff Summary\r\n\r\n| Metric | Count |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Added | 0 |\r\n| **Modified** | **1** |\r\n| Removed | 0 |\r\n\r\nThe single modified resource is `ClusterRole/demo-app-reader`. The candidate changed:\r\n\r\n| Field | Baseline | Candidate |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `apiGroups` | `[\"\"]` | `[\"*\"]` |\r\n| `resources` | `[\"pods\", \"services\"]` | `[\"*\"]` |\r\n| `verbs` | `[\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]` | `[\"*\"]` |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Proposed Fix (Minimal Code Change)\r\n\r\nThe candidate's `rbac.yaml` must replace the wildcard rules with explicit, least-privilege values matching the baseline intent. The smallest concrete fix:\r\n\r\n**File:** `examples/rbac-escalation/candidate/templates/rbac.yaml`\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\n# BEFORE (candidate — BLOCKS)\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"*\"]\r\n    resources: [\"*\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"*\"]\r\n\r\n# AFTER (fixed — will PASS)\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"\"]\r\n    resources: [\"pods\", \"services\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n- **RBAC-001 fix**: Replace `resources: [\"*\"]` with the explicit list `[\"pods\", \"services\"]`\r\n- **RBAC-002 fix**: Replace `verbs: [\"*\"]` with the explicit list `[\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]`\r\n- **apiGroups fix**: Replace `[\"*\"]` with `[\"\"]` (core API group only)\r\n\r\n> ⚠️ Per the skill protocol, **human authorization is required** before modifying any project file. The fix is proposed here for review — not applied.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Which Example Would Pass Instead?\r\n\r\nThe **`examples/safe-upgrade/`** example would pass. Its candidate chart (`safe-upgrade/candidate/templates/deployment.yaml`) only modifies a `Deployment` resource — bumping the nginx image tag. It contains **no RBAC resources at all**, so neither RBAC-001 nor RBAC-002 can fire. The diff would be a single image field change on a Deployment, which carries no RBAC policy risk and would yield a **PASS** verdict.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Summary\r\n\r\n```\r\nPreflight verdict: BLOCK — upgrade must not proceed\r\n\r\nFindings:\r\n  [CRITICAL] RBAC-001 (new): ClusterRole/demo-app-reader\r\n    Path: $.rules[0].resources\r\n    Wildcard (*) in resources grants access to all resource types\r\n\r\n  [CRITICAL] RBAC-002 (new): ClusterRole/demo-app-reader\r\n    Path: $.rules[0].verbs\r\n    Wildcard (*) in verbs grants all operations\r\n\r\nFingerprint: 80483bd4091749dd4b4f9b7642d832e761bbe24d30decc2c57343027e3453142\r\nNo deployment occurred: confirmed ✅\r\nEvidence: COMPLETE — rendering stable ✅\r\n```\r\n"]
